


{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Diet Study – Human Gut Microbiome EDA\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** knights-lab/dietstudy_analyses  \n",
    "**Study design:** Longitudinal dietary intervention — 37 participants, ~17 study days each  \n",
    "**Two supplement arms:** MCT oil vs. Extra-Virgin Olive Oil (EVOO)  \n",
    "**Microbiome profiling:** 16S rRNA amplicon sequencing of fecal samples  \n",
    "\n",
    "**Research goal:** Quantify how exposure to food microbiomes affects key features of the human gut ecosystem — stability, diversity, and overall community structure."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid', palette='muted')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.dpi'] = 120\n",
    "\n",
    "BASE_DIR = 'dietstudy_data'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Loading the Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- Sample-level metadata (643 rows x 29 columns) ---\n",
    "sample_map = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE_DIR}/maps/SampleID_map.txt', sep='\\t')\n",
    "sample_map.rename(columns={'#SampleID': 'SampleID'}, inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Participant-level metadata (37 participants x 45 columns) ---\n",
    "user_map = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE_DIR}/maps/UserName_map.txt', sep='\\t')\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Microbiome: BURST taxonomy table (taxa x samples, raw counts) ---\n",
    "# rows = taxa (full lineage string), columns = sample IDs\n",
    "burst = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE_DIR}/microbiome/BURST.tax.txt', sep='\\t', index_col=0)\n",
    "burst.index.name = 'taxonomy'\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Nutritional data (65 nutrients x samples) ---\n",
    "# rows = nutrient features, columns = sample IDs\n",
    "nutr_raw = pd.read_csv(f'{BASE_DIR}/diet/nutr_65.txt', sep='\\t', index_col=0)\n",
    "nutr_raw.index.name = 'nutrient'\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Loaded successfully.')\n",
    "print(f'  sample_map:  {sample_map.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'  user_map:    {user_map.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'  burst:       {burst.shape}  (taxa x samples)')\n",
    "print(f'  nutr_raw:    {nutr_raw.shape}  (nutrients x samples)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## About the Data\n",
    "\n",
    "The raw microbiome table (`BURST.tax.txt`) and the nutritional table (`nutr_65.txt`) are both oriented **features × samples** (rows = features, columns = samples).\n",
    "The metadata tables (`SampleID_map`, `UserName_map`) are oriented **samples × metadata** (rows = samples or participants).\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: `SampleID_map` also contains blank and control rows — we will filter to only valid fecal samples below."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "display(sample_map.head(3))\n",
    "display(user_map.head(3))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Filtering: Keep Only Valid Fecal Samples\n",
    "\n",
    "The `SampleID_map` contains blank controls and non-fecal rows. We keep only rows where:\n",
    "- `fecal.status == 1` (confirmed stool sample)\n",
    "- `UserName` starts with `MCTs` (actual study participants, not blanks)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fecal_map = sample_map[\n",
    "    (sample_map['fecal.status'] == 1) &\n",
    "    (sample_map['UserName'].str.startswith('MCTs', na=False))\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Total rows in sample_map:     {len(sample_map)}')\n",
    "print(f'Valid fecal samples retained: {len(fecal_map)}')\n",
    "print(f'Unique participants:          {fecal_map[\"UserName\"].nunique()}')\n",
    "print(f'Study days covered:           {fecal_map[\"StudyDayNo\"].nunique()}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Study Design Overview"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Supplement arm distribution (participant level)\n",
    "supp_counts = user_map['Supplement'].value_counts()\n",
    "axes[0].bar(supp_counts.index, supp_counts.values, color=['#4C72B0', '#DD8452'])\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Participants per Supplement Arm')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Number of Participants')\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(supp_counts.values):\n",
    "    axes[0].text(i, v + 0.2, str(v), ha='center', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Gender distribution\n",
    "gender_counts = user_map['Gender'].value_counts()\n",
    "axes[1].pie(gender_counts.values, labels=gender_counts.index, autopct='%1.0f%%',\n",
    "            colors=['#4C72B0', '#DD8452'], startangle=90)\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Gender Distribution (n=37)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Age distribution\n",
    "axes[2].hist(user_map['Age'].dropna(), bins=10, color='#55A868', edgecolor='white')\n",
    "axes[2].set_title('Age Distribution')\n",
    "axes[2].set_xlabel('Age (years)')\n",
    "axes[2].set_ylabel('Count')\n",
    "axes[2].axvline(user_map['Age'].mean(), color='red', linestyle='--', label=f\"Mean: {user_map['Age'].mean():.1f}\")\n",
    "axes[2].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Study Design – Participant Overview', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Samples per participant across study days\n",
    "samples_per_participant = fecal_map.groupby('UserName')['StudyDayNo'].count().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].bar(range(len(samples_per_participant)), samples_per_participant.values, color='#4C72B0')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Fecal Samples per Participant')\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('Participant (sorted)')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Number of Samples')\n",
    "axes[0].axhline(samples_per_participant.mean(), color='red', linestyle='--',\n",
    "                label=f'Mean: {samples_per_participant.mean():.1f}')\n",
    "axes[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Samples per study day\n",
    "samples_per_day = fecal_map.groupby('StudyDayNo')['SampleID'].count()\n",
    "axes[1].bar(samples_per_day.index, samples_per_day.values, color='#55A868')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Fecal Samples per Study Day')\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('Study Day Number')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Number of Samples')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Longitudinal Sampling Overview', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Study day range: {fecal_map[\"StudyDayNo\"].min()} – {fecal_map[\"StudyDayNo\"].max()}')\n",
    "print(f'Mean samples per participant: {samples_per_participant.mean():.1f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Missing Values Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def plot_missing(df, title, ax):\n",
    "    missing = (df.isnull().mean() * 100).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "    missing = missing[missing > 0]\n",
    "    if missing.empty:\n",
    "        ax.text(0.5, 0.5, 'No missing values', ha='center', va='center', transform=ax.transAxes, fontsize=12)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(title)\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    ax.barh(missing.index, missing.values, color='#C44E52')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Missing (%)')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(title)\n",
    "    ax.axvline(5, color='orange', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7, label='5% threshold')\n",
    "    ax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "plot_missing(fecal_map, 'Missing Values – Sample Metadata (fecal only)', axes[0])\n",
    "plot_missing(user_map, 'Missing Values – Participant Metadata', axes[1])\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Microbiome Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "Steps:\n",
    "1. Keep only the fecal sample columns in the BURST table\n",
    "2. Convert raw counts → relative abundance (%) per sample\n",
    "3. Filter taxa with mean relative abundance < 0.01% (noise removal)\n",
    "4. Extract species-level (s__) profiles for downstream analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Keep only fecal sample columns present in both burst and fecal_map\n",
    "fecal_ids = fecal_map['SampleID'].tolist()\n",
    "shared_ids = [s for s in fecal_ids if s in burst.columns]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Fecal sample IDs in metadata:     {len(fecal_ids)}')\n",
    "print(f'Found in BURST table:             {len(shared_ids)}')\n",
    "print(f'Missing from BURST (not sequenced): {len(fecal_ids) - len(shared_ids)}')\n",
    "\n",
    "burst_fecal = burst[shared_ids].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Normalize to relative abundance (%)\n",
    "burst_rel = burst_fecal.div(burst_fecal.sum(axis=0), axis=1) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter low-abundance taxa (mean < 0.01% across all samples)\n",
    "mean_abund = burst_rel.mean(axis=1)\n",
    "burst_filtered = burst_rel[mean_abund >= 0.01]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Taxa before filtering: {len(burst_rel)}')\n",
    "print(f'Taxa after filtering (mean >= 0.01%): {len(burst_filtered)}')\n",
    "print(f'Retained: {len(burst_filtered)/len(burst_rel)*100:.1f}% of taxa, '\n",
    "      f'covering ~{burst_filtered.sum().mean():.1f}% of reads on average')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract species-level taxa (rows containing 's__' but not 't__')\n",
    "is_species = burst_filtered.index.str.contains(';s__') & ~burst_filtered.index.str.contains(';t__')\n",
    "burst_species = burst_filtered[is_species].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Shorten taxa names: keep only the species part\n",
    "def short_name(full_taxa):\n",
    "    parts = full_taxa.split(';')\n",
    "    return parts[-1].replace('s__', '').replace('_', ' ')\n",
    "\n",
    "burst_species.index = burst_species.index.map(short_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Species-level taxa: {len(burst_species)}')\n",
    "display(burst_species.iloc[:5, :4])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Taxonomic Composition Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "Top 10 most abundant genera across all fecal samples."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract genus-level taxa\n",
    "is_genus = burst_filtered.index.str.contains(';g__') & ~burst_filtered.index.str.contains(';s__')\n",
    "burst_genus = burst_filtered[is_genus].copy()\n",
    "burst_genus.index = burst_genus.index.map(lambda x: x.split(';g__')[-1].replace('_', ' '))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Top 10 genera by mean relative abundance\n",
    "top10_genera = burst_genus.mean(axis=1).sort_values(ascending=False).head(10)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Bar chart of top 10\n",
    "axes[0].barh(top10_genera.index[::-1], top10_genera.values[::-1], color=sns.color_palette('tab10', 10))\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('Mean Relative Abundance (%)')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Top 10 Genera (Mean Abundance)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pie chart of composition\n",
    "other = 100 - top10_genera.sum()\n",
    "pie_vals = list(top10_genera.values) + [other]\n",
    "pie_labels = list(top10_genera.index) + ['Other']\n",
    "colors = sns.color_palette('tab10', 10) + ['#cccccc']\n",
    "axes[1].pie(pie_vals, labels=pie_labels, autopct='%1.1f%%', colors=colors,\n",
    "            textprops={'fontsize': 8}, startangle=90)\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Genus-level Composition')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Gut Microbiome – Taxonomic Composition (All Fecal Samples)', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Alpha Diversity\n",
    "\n",
    "Alpha diversity measures **within-sample** diversity. We compute:\n",
    "- **Shannon entropy** — accounts for both richness and evenness\n",
    "- **Observed species** — number of species with abundance > 0"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def shannon_entropy(col):\n",
    "    p = col[col > 0] / 100  # convert % to proportion\n",
    "    return -np.sum(p * np.log(p))\n",
    "\n",
    "def observed_species(col):\n",
    "    return (col > 0).sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "alpha_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'SampleID': burst_species.columns,\n",
    "    'shannon':  burst_species.apply(shannon_entropy, axis=0).values,\n",
    "    'observed': burst_species.apply(observed_species, axis=0).values\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Merge with sample metadata\n",
    "alpha_df = alpha_df.merge(fecal_map[['SampleID', 'UserName', 'StudyDayNo', 'Supplement']], on='SampleID', how='left')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Alpha diversity computed for {len(alpha_df)} samples')\n",
    "print(f'Shannon entropy — mean: {alpha_df[\"shannon\"].mean():.2f}, std: {alpha_df[\"shannon\"].std():.2f}')\n",
    "print(f'Observed species — mean: {alpha_df[\"observed\"].mean():.1f}, std: {alpha_df[\"observed\"].std():.1f}')\n",
    "display(alpha_df.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, metric, label in zip(axes, ['shannon', 'observed'], ['Shannon Entropy', 'Observed Species']):\n",
    "    ax.hist(alpha_df[metric].dropna(), bins=25, color='#4C72B0', edgecolor='white')\n",
    "    ax.axvline(alpha_df[metric].mean(), color='red', linestyle='--',\n",
    "               label=f'Mean: {alpha_df[metric].mean():.2f}')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(label)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Number of Samples')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'Distribution of {label}')\n",
    "    ax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Alpha Diversity – All Fecal Samples', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Alpha Diversity by Supplement Arm (MCT vs. EVOO)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "palette = {'MCT': '#4C72B0', 'EVOO': '#DD8452'}\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, metric, label in zip(axes, ['shannon', 'observed'], ['Shannon Entropy', 'Observed Species']):\n",
    "    data_clean = alpha_df[alpha_df['Supplement'].isin(['MCT', 'EVOO'])]\n",
    "    sns.boxplot(data=data_clean, x='Supplement', y=metric, palette=palette, ax=ax, width=0.5)\n",
    "    sns.stripplot(data=data_clean, x='Supplement', y=metric, palette=palette,\n",
    "                  ax=ax, alpha=0.3, jitter=True, size=3)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'{label} by Supplement Arm')\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(label)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Print group means\n",
    "    for supp in ['MCT', 'EVOO']:\n",
    "        m = data_clean[data_clean['Supplement'] == supp][metric].mean()\n",
    "        print(f'  {label} — {supp}: mean = {m:.3f}')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Alpha Diversity: MCT Oil vs. EVOO', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Alpha Diversity Over Study Days (Longitudinal)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "alpha_by_day = alpha_df[alpha_df['Supplement'].isin(['MCT', 'EVOO'])].groupby(\n",
    "    ['StudyDayNo', 'Supplement']\n",
    )[['shannon', 'observed']].mean().reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, metric, label in zip(axes, ['shannon', 'observed'], ['Shannon Entropy', 'Observed Species']):\n",
    "    for supp, color in palette.items():\n",
    "        d = alpha_by_day[alpha_by_day['Supplement'] == supp].sort_values('StudyDayNo')\n",
    "        ax.plot(d['StudyDayNo'], d[metric], marker='o', label=supp, color=color, linewidth=2, markersize=4)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Study Day')\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(f'Mean {label}')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'{label} Over Study Days')\n",
    "    ax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Longitudinal Alpha Diversity by Supplement Arm', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Nutritional Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "The `nutr_65.txt` file contains 65 nutritional features (e.g. KCAL, PROT, fiber types) per sample.  \n",
    "We transpose it so rows = samples, then merge with metadata to compare arms."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Transpose: rows = samples, cols = nutrients\n",
    "nutr = nutr_raw.T.copy()\n",
    "nutr.index.name = 'SampleID'\n",
    "nutr = nutr.reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Merge with sample metadata\n",
    "nutr = nutr.merge(fecal_map[['SampleID', 'UserName', 'StudyDayNo', 'Supplement']], on='SampleID', how='inner')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Nutritional data after merge: {nutr.shape}')\n",
    "display(nutr[['SampleID', 'UserName', 'Supplement', 'StudyDayNo', 'KCAL', 'PROT']].head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Key macronutrients comparison: MCT vs EVOO\n",
    "key_nutrients = ['KCAL', 'PROT', 'TFAT', 'CARB', 'FIBE']\n",
    "key_nutrients = [n for n in key_nutrients if n in nutr.columns]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(key_nutrients), figsize=(4 * len(key_nutrients), 4))\n",
    "if len(key_nutrients) == 1:\n",
    "    axes = [axes]\n",
    "\n",
    "data_clean = nutr[nutr['Supplement'].isin(['MCT', 'EVOO'])]\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, nutrient in zip(axes, key_nutrients):\n",
    "    sns.boxplot(data=data_clean, x='Supplement', y=nutrient, palette=palette, ax=ax, width=0.5)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(nutrient)\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Key Macronutrients by Supplement Arm', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Distribution of caloric intake across the study\n",
    "if 'KCAL' in nutr.columns:\n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "    axes[0].hist(data_clean['KCAL'].dropna(), bins=30, color='#55A868', edgecolor='white')\n",
    "    axes[0].axvline(data_clean['KCAL'].mean(), color='red', linestyle='--',\n",
    "                    label=f'Mean: {data_clean[\"KCAL\"].mean():.0f} kcal')\n",
    "    axes[0].set_xlabel('Daily Caloric Intake (kcal)')\n",
    "    axes[0].set_ylabel('Samples')\n",
    "    axes[0].set_title('Caloric Intake Distribution')\n",
    "    axes[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "    kcal_by_day = data_clean.groupby(['StudyDayNo', 'Supplement'])['KCAL'].mean().reset_index()\n",
    "    for supp, color in palette.items():\n",
